<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="020" project="spaarkeai-compose-r6">
  <metadata>
    <title>Canonical document model — generalize ComposeContentModel/projection as the single hub between every source and the editor</title>
    <phase>2 Canonical model + fidelity widening</phase>
    <gate>startable — deps 001 (ADR-049 Path-B amendment, committed on branch) + 004 (NDA fixture). RE-SEQUENCED 2026-08-05: this is the render-on-save ANCHOR (was gated on 014; that was a dependency inversion — see plan.md §5 banner). Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Architectural pivot: generalizes the editor projection into THE canonical hub every downstream fidelity task (021-026) builds on. Modifies shared Services/Compose files on the most-contested BFF surface; a wrong model shape cascades into every feature adapter. FR-03 core. code-review + adr-check run at Step 9.5 (FULL/BFF/architecture).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Per plan.md §5 Phase 2 — high-blast-radius architectural generalization of the canonical model; deep OOXML/model-shape reasoning that anchors the whole phase; opus tier assigned in the plan.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits shared Services/Compose files (ComposeContentModel / ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder / ComposeDocumentRenderer) — the MOST-CONTESTED repo surface. Overlaps spaarkeai-compose-r5/r4.5/r3/r2/r1 + spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2 + ai-advanced-capabilities-agreements-r1/analysis-hub-r1. Anchor task of Phase 2; every 021-026 adapter serializes behind it. Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001, 004</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, compose</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 weeks</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Generalize the existing editor projection (ComposeContentModel / ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder) into the single
    canonical document model that sits between EVERY source format and the editor: every source becomes the model,
    the editor edits the model, and save renders the model out (FR-03). This is an EXTENSION of the existing
    projection — not a new model type. Reuse the R4.5 NumberingComputationEngine (ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs:1357)
    for numbering. Prove docx projects into the canonical model and the model renders back out through
    ComposeDocumentRenderer.SynthesizeDocument on the render-on-save path with no hard-fail.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in OOXML (DocumentFormat.OpenXml 3.5.1), the Compose canonical projection (ComposeContentModel), the render-from-model author (ComposeDocumentRenderer), and the render-on-save architecture codified by the ADR-049 Path-B amendment. Follow ADRs strictly; keep Services/Compose byte[]-in / projection-out.</role>

  <goal>ComposeContentModel is generalized into the single canonical hub: docx projects into it via ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder, the editor edits it, and ComposeDocumentRenderer.SynthesizeDocument renders it back to a fresh docx on the save path. The model is source-agnostic (docx today, PDF-ready by shape for Phase 4), reuses NumberingComputationEngine for numbering, and persists per ADR-040. A seam slice proves docx → canonical model → render round-trips without hard-fail and the NDA fixture still saves (no 422). No new parallel model type is introduced; the existing projection is extended.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-03 (canonical document model): the render-on-save pivot (Phase 1) routes all saves through render-from-model; Phase 2 makes the model the single hub so every source format (docx now, PDF in Phase 4) and every fidelity feature (021-026) flows through one representation. The R4.5 NumberingComputationEngine (deterministic, numId-scoped per ECMA-376) is reused, not re-implemented. This is the Phase-2 anchor: 021-026 each widen a feature THROUGH this model.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/docxBridge.ts</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Compose/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="complete">ADR-049 Path-B amendment codifying render-on-save (committed on this branch; merges with this code).</dependency>
      <dependency task="004" status="complete">NDA fixture in tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/ (LFS) — the round-trip + no-422 oracle for this task's seam slice.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <!-- RE-SEQUENCED 2026-08-05 (owner-authorized): this task is the render-on-save ANCHOR and runs FIRST among the
         code tasks. A Step-2 trace on task 010 found that render-from-model has no faithful canonical-model SOURCE for
         imported docs until THIS task builds the docx→canonical-model projection; the cutover (010/011/012) now depends
         on 020 + 026, not the reverse. See notes/task-010-resequence-decision.md + plan.md §5/§6. -->

  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Save renders a fresh docx from the canonical model per the Path-B amendment (task 001) — NO surgical byte-patch and NO text-search on the save path. The canonical model is the single source the renderer authors from; version history is the fidelity safety net.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Services/Compose stays byte[]-in / projection-out; NO Microsoft.Graph types above SpeFileStore. The canonical model is a pure in-memory projection.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">No AI-internal types (IOpenAiClient / executors / routing) in Services/Compose (Tier-1 NetArchTest). Consume Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ seams only — NO fork of Services/Ai (sole owner: spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Engine frozen — add NO new AI dispatch endpoint. The canonical model is a projection/render concern, not a dispatch surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Persist the canonical model / projection payload per the existing session-ledger pattern; do not invent a new persistence channel.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Add through-the-wire WebApplicationFactory seam slices in tests/integration/seam/Compose/. NO Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, NO DI-registration tests, NO ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029/010">Report absolute BFF publish size + delta vs ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs baseline (re-measured task 003); ≤60 MB compressed ceiling; minimal DI (no new singletons unless justified).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NEVER delete docxBridge.ts (exports buildContentModel/stampParaIds/paraId helpers the write path depends on — only the mammoth READ fn was removed in R4.5). Reuse NumberingComputationEngine (ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs:1357) — do NOT re-implement. Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR; state Placement Justification citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Compose canonical model + render-on-save</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/plan.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Render-from-model author" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs">SynthesizeDocument:102 (render-from-model precedent) / AppendSection:142 (author-not-patch) — the canonical model must render out through this author on the save path.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Numbering engine (reuse)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs">NumberingComputationEngine:1357 — deterministic, numId-scoped; reuse for numbering in the canonical model, do not re-implement.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Save-path discriminant" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs">SaveAsync:642, Authored/Imported branch :714 — both branches now render the canonical model.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbors: ComposeContentModel + ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs (the existing editor projection) and ComposeDocumentRenderer.SynthesizeDocument:102 (the existing render-from-model author). A projection already exists — this task generalizes it, it does not introduce a parallel model.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — EXTEND the existing ComposeContentModel/projection into the single source-agnostic hub. Not a new model type, not a new service. Per spec §"New Components": render-on-save routing and the canonical model are explicitly "modify/extend existing → no new-component justification required"; this brief justification is stated per the operator directive since the model is broadened.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without one canonical hub, each source (docx, PDF) and each fidelity feature (021-026) would need its own projection/render pairing — the exact fan-out that produced the R3→R5 anchor bug class. FR-03 acceptance (docx and PDF projecting into the same model; golden-label numbering parity) cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load all knowledge files. Declare RIGOR LEVEL FULL + reason. Confirm 001 (ADR-049 amendment, committed on branch) + 004 (NDA fixture) are present. NOTE (re-sequence 2026-08-05): this is the FIRST render-on-save code task — do NOT wait on 010/014; the docx→canonical-model projection built here is the prerequisite the cutover (010) depends on. Run /conflict-check for Services/Compose.</step>
    <step order="1">Read ComposeContentModel + ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs and ComposeDocumentRenderer.SynthesizeDocument:102 / AppendSection:142. Map the current projection shape and where it is source-specific (docx-only assumptions) vs source-agnostic.</step>
    <step order="2">Generalize ComposeContentModel into the single canonical hub: a source-agnostic block/inline model that docx projects INTO (via ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder) and that renders OUT via ComposeDocumentRenderer.SynthesizeDocument. Keep it PDF-ready by shape (Phase 4) without building PDF intake here.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire numbering through NumberingComputationEngine (ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs:1357) — reuse, do not re-implement. Ensure numbering labels are computed deterministically (numId-scoped).</step>
    <step order="4">Ensure ComposeService.SaveAsync (:642 / :714) renders the canonical model out on both branches on the render-on-save path; persist the canonical-model/projection payload per ADR-040.</step>
    <step order="5">Add a seam slice in tests/integration/seam/Compose/: docx → canonical model → render round-trips without hard-fail; the NDA fixture saves (no 422) and produces a new SPE version.</step>
    <step order="6">Run dotnet publish -c Release; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB (incl. PDBs). Run /conflict-check; state Placement Justification in the PR.</step>
    <step order="7">Run/verify: BFF build + this task's seam slice + Tier-1 NetArchTest pass.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If generalizing ComposeContentModel would require introducing a second/parallel model type (not an extension of the existing projection), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §11 / §6.5 — the directive is extend-not-new.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the render-on-save path would need text-search or surgical anchoring to render the canonical model faithfully, STOP (ADR-049 Path-B amendment: no text-search / no surgical anchoring on the save path).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish the BFF; run the seam slice + Tier-1 NetArchTest.</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs (generalized canonical model)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs (render-out of canonical model on save)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ (docx → canonical model → render round-trip)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a corpus docx, when it is projected then rendered on the save path, then it round-trips through the single canonical ComposeContentModel without hard-fail and produces a new immutable SPE version.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the NDA fixture, when saved after an edit, then it succeeds (no 422) with no surgical-anchor code on the save path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the corpus numbering exemplars, when projected through the canonical model, then numbering labels match Word (R4.5 golden labels) via the reused NumberingComputationEngine.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the canonical model, then it is source-agnostic by shape (no docx-only coupling that blocks a future PDF projection) — verified by the model's public shape, not by building PDF intake.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative / no-regression: no new parallel model type is introduced (extension only); Tier-1 NetArchTest passes (no AI internals in Services/Compose); docxBridge.ts is not deleted; BFF publish ≤60 MB with delta reported vs ~49.63 MB; seam slice uses no banned mock/DI/ctor shapes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-03; plan.md §5 Phase 2 (anchor task) + §6 critical path (014 → 020 → 027). EXTEND the existing projection — justification emitted above. Phase-2 anchor: 021-026 build on this model; 027 seam-tests them. parallel-safe=false (most-contested Compose surface). Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt; first. Follow task-execute pre-execution checklist incl. Step 9.5 gates (code-review + adr-check, FULL/BFF). Enforce §10 publish-size gate and /conflict-check.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
